  <items>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp167336504">lap (pl. lapan)</headword>
      <description>Quotation: Bha lapan sa bhuntàta far nach do dh’fhàs iad idir. Notes: patches where potatoes had failed to grow.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp167338160">ploc-fàl</headword>
      <description>Notes: one piece of turf specially cut to cover a new grave.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp167339744">broth</headword>
      <description>Notes: rash on the skin, as with measles.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp167341256">cloimh</headword>
      <description>Notes: mange (in dogs).</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp167342768">dìobair</headword>
      <description>Quotation: Tha i glé mhath mara dìobair i. Notes: Alleged to have been said by some woman to ‘MacCoinnich’ of Ioscaig when he had boasted of a bridge he had just made. Sense of ‘fail, give way’.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp167344424">faofag</headword>
      <description>Quotation: pl. faofagan. Notes: ‘Squid’.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp167346080">giobarnach</headword>
      <description>Notes: octopus (‘Lewis form’).</description>
    </item>
